From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:34:32 -0800
Subject: [PDF] Prevent page unloading in PDFiumPage::GenerateThumbnail()

PDFs with JS can potentially trigger page unloading while
GenerateThumbnail() is rendering. Use ScopedPageUnloadPreventer to make
sure that does not happen.

Bug: 579818899
Change-Id: I7525abd9f21a678510318493e32523a08f231574
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8694663
Reviewed-by: Tom Sepez <tsepez@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Tom Sepez <tsepez@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733082}

diff --git a/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc b/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
index a79e744fc8e073a05fa50251c24368d224bb73fe..901661db7a6a98b542f9ec0adf9b950357902b4f 100644
--- a/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
+++ b/pdf/pdfium/pdfium_page.cc
@@ -2052,6 +2052,9 @@ Thumbnail PDFiumPage::GenerateThumbnail(float device_pixel_ratio) {
   DCHECK(available());
 
   FPDF_PAGE page = GetPage();
+  // Make sure `page` stays valid for the duration of this function.
+  ScopedPageUnloadPreventer scoped_unload_preventer(this);
+
   const bool has_alpha = !!FPDFPage_HasTransparency(page);
   const int format = has_alpha ? FPDFBitmap_BGRA : FPDFBitmap_BGRx;
 
